{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Semantic Segmentation \u2014 U-Net Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Encoder block"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two 3x3 convs with batch norm and ReLU. The first conv changes channel count; the second keeps it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class DoubleConv(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_c, out_c):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.net = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(in_c, out_c, kernel_size=3, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(out_c),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(out_c, out_c, kernel_size=3, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(out_c),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This block is reused throughout. `bias=False` because BN's beta handles the bias."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Down and up blocks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Down(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_c, out_c):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.net = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.MaxPool2d(2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            DoubleConv(in_c, out_c),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Up(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_c, out_c):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.up = nn.Upsample(scale_factor=2, mode=\"bilinear\", align_corners=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv = DoubleConv(in_c, out_c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x, skip):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.up(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if x.shape[-2:] != skip.shape[-2:]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = F.interpolate(x, size=skip.shape[-2:], mode=\"bilinear\", align_corners=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = torch.cat([skip, x], dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.conv(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The spatial-only shape check (`shape[-2:]`) handles inputs whose dimensions are not divisible by 16; a safe `F.interpolate` aligns the tensor before the concat. Comparing the full shape would also trigger on channel-count differences, which should be a loud error, not a silent interpolate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: The U-Net"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class UNet(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels=3, num_classes=2, base=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.inc = DoubleConv(in_channels, base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.d1 = Down(base, base * 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.d2 = Down(base * 2, base * 4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.d3 = Down(base * 4, base * 8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.d4 = Down(base * 8, base * 16)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.u1 = Up(base * 16 + base * 8, base * 8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.u2 = Up(base * 8 + base * 4, base * 4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.u3 = Up(base * 4 + base * 2, base * 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.u4 = Up(base * 2 + base, base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.outc = nn.Conv2d(base, num_classes, kernel_size=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x1 = self.inc(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x2 = self.d1(x1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x3 = self.d2(x2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x4 = self.d3(x3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x5 = self.d4(x4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.u1(x5, x4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.u2(x, x3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.u3(x, x2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.u4(x, x1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.outc(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net = UNet(in_channels=3, num_classes=2, base=32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(1, 3, 256, 256)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output: {net(x).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in net.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output shape `(1, 2, 256, 256)` \u2014 same spatial size as the input, `num_classes` channels. About 7.7M parameters at `base=32`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Losses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def dice_loss(logits, targets, num_classes, eps=1e-6):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = F.softmax(logits, dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    targets_one_hot = F.one_hot(targets, num_classes).permute(0, 3, 1, 2).float()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dims = (0, 2, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    intersection = (probs * targets_one_hot).sum(dim=dims)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    denom = probs.sum(dim=dims) + targets_one_hot.sum(dim=dims)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dice = (2 * intersection + eps) / (denom + eps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1 - dice.mean()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def combined_loss(logits, targets, num_classes, lam=1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ce = F.cross_entropy(logits, targets)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dc = dice_loss(logits, targets, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return ce + lam * dc, {\"ce\": ce.item(), \"dice\": dc.item()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Dice is computed per class then averaged (macro Dice). The `eps` prevents division by zero on classes absent from the batch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: IoU metric"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@torch.no_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def iou_per_class(logits, targets, num_classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    preds = logits.argmax(dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ious = torch.zeros(num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for c in range(num_classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred_c = (preds == c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        true_c = (targets == c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        inter = (pred_c & true_c).sum().float()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        union = (pred_c | true_c).sum().float()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ious[c] = (inter / union) if union > 0 else torch.tensor(float(\"nan\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return ious"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Returns a vector of length C. `nan` marks classes absent from the batch \u2014 do not average over those when computing mIoU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Synthetic dataset for end-to-end verification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Generate shapes on coloured backgrounds so the network has to learn shape, not pixel colour."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_segmentation(num_samples=200, size=64, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    images = np.zeros((num_samples, size, size, 3), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    masks = np.zeros((num_samples, size, size), dtype=np.int64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(num_samples):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        bg = rng.uniform(0, 1, (3,))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        images[i] = bg"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        masks[i] = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_shapes = rng.integers(1, 4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(num_shapes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            cls = int(rng.integers(1, 3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            color = rng.uniform(0, 1, (3,))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            cx, cy = rng.integers(10, size - 10, size=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            r = int(rng.integers(4, 12))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            yy, xx = np.meshgrid(np.arange(size), np.arange(size), indexing=\"ij\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if cls == 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                mask = (xx - cx) ** 2 + (yy - cy) ** 2 < r ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                mask = (np.abs(xx - cx) < r) & (np.abs(yy - cy) < r)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            images[i][mask] = color"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            masks[i][mask] = cls"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        images[i] += rng.normal(0, 0.02, images[i].shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        images[i] = np.clip(images[i], 0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return images, masks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SegDataset(Dataset):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, images, masks):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.images = images"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.masks = masks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __len__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return len(self.images)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __getitem__(self, i):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        img = torch.from_numpy(self.images[i]).permute(2, 0, 1).float()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mask = torch.from_numpy(self.masks[i]).long()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return img, mask"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three classes: background (0), circles (1), squares (2). The network must learn to distinguish shape."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Training loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_one_epoch(model, loader, optimizer, device, num_classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_sum, total = 0.0, 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    iou_sum = torch.zeros(num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for x, y in loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x, y = x.to(device), y.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = model(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss, _ = combined_loss(logits, y, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss_sum += loss.item() * x.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += x.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        iou_sum += iou_per_class(logits, y, num_classes).nan_to_num(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss_sum / total, iou_sum / len(loader)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
